1069 "e-14476" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171739 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $31^2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171739 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "53a23554-58d8-595a-8e14-bd36e00f678d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171739 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate $31^2,$ we start by writing it out with a multiplication sign:\n![](images/0f/0f6a4e089111de1dbb0e16cb6c388d3dcd236e981f94e2b4694c3492e3d526a3.svg)\n\nThen, we work out $31 \\times 31.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $31 \\times 31 =   961.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171759 #edb/ref 1069 "e-15038" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171759 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $220^2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171759 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "60c9af0c-e7f2-5027-855b-dcc5868e3ee3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171759 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate $220^2,$ we start by writing it out with a multiplication sign:\n![](images/e9/e963c6c194b0cf3991be02d43f130eb81cd3e6f16b1b6921718468b3752ddc07.svg)\n\nThen, we work out $220 \\times 220.$\n\nFirst, we figure out the non-zero part and the block of zeros for both numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}220 & \\,⟶\\,220 \\\\ 220 & \\,⟶\\,220\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can see that there are $2$ zeros in total.\n\nNext, we multiply the non-zero parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \